### LocalMind AI — REST Client Test Suite
### Use with VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
### Run requests top-to-bottom; copy the token from /auth/login into @token below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@contentType = application/json

# After logging in, paste your token here:
@token = PASTE_YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE


# =============================================================================
# HEALTH CHECK
# =============================================================================

### Health check — should return {"status": "ok"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: {{contentType}}


# =============================================================================
# AUTH
# =============================================================================

### 1. Register a new user
# Expected: 201 Created with user object
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "testuser@localmind.ai",
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}


###

### 2. Login — copy the access_token value into @token above
# Expected: 200 OK with {"access_token": "...", "token_type": "bearer"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "testuser@localmind.ai",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}


###

### 3. Get current user profile (requires Bearer token)
# Expected: 200 OK with user object
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


###

### 4. Register duplicate — should fail
# Expected: 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "testuser@localmind.ai",
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}


# =============================================================================
# CHAT — Models
# =============================================================================

### 5. List available LLM models and their online/offline status
# Expected: 200 OK with array of model objects
GET {{baseUrl}}/chat/models
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


# =============================================================================
# CHAT — Conversations
# =============================================================================

### 6. Send a message (streaming SSE)
# Expected: 200 text/event-stream with "data: {...}" lines
# The X-Conversation-Id response header contains the new conversation UUID.
# NOTE: REST Client shows the stream as it arrives.
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/send
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "model_name": "llama3",
  "message": "Hello! What can you help me with today?",
  "rag_enabled": false
}


###

### 7. Send a follow-up message in the same conversation
# Replace CONVERSATION_ID with the UUID from the X-Conversation-Id header above
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/send
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "conversation_id": "CONVERSATION_ID",
  "model_name": "llama3",
  "message": "Can you explain what RAG is?",
  "rag_enabled": false
}


###

### 8. List all conversations
# Expected: 200 OK with array of conversation objects
GET {{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


###

### 9. Get a specific conversation with messages
# Replace CONVERSATION_ID with a real UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations/CONVERSATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


###

### 10. Delete a conversation
# Expected: 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations/CONVERSATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


# =============================================================================
# VOICE (requires Whisper + Coqui TTS installed)
# =============================================================================

### 11. Synthesize text-to-speech
# Expected: 200 OK with audio/wav binary response (downloads as speech.wav)
POST {{baseUrl}}/voice/synthesize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "text": "Hello! I am LocalMind, your local AI assistant."
}


# NOTE: /voice/transcribe requires a multipart file upload.
# Use the following curl command from a terminal instead:
#
# curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/voice/transcribe \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" \
#   -F "audio=@/path/to/your/audio.wav"


# =============================================================================
# RAG — Documents
# =============================================================================

### 12. List uploaded documents
# Expected: 200 OK with array (empty if none uploaded yet)
GET {{baseUrl}}/rag/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


# NOTE: /rag/upload requires a multipart PDF upload.
# Use the following curl command from a terminal instead:
#
# curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/rag/upload \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" \
#   -F "file=@/path/to/your/document.pdf"


### 13. Delete a document
# Replace DOCUMENT_ID with a real UUID from /rag/documents
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rag/documents/DOCUMENT_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


###

### 14. Chat with a document (RAG)
# Replace DOCUMENT_ID with a UUID of a "ready" document
POST {{baseUrl}}/rag/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "document_id": "DOCUMENT_ID",
  "model_name": "llama3",
  "message": "What is this document about?"
}
